%U A399790 1244606503041737989522973687270307004416,7527497766053731495116095050019129945409346185723904,2475439037964637346631594200752422795364624353210547235207730167808
%N A399790 Number of spanning trees in the knight graph on an n X n chessboard.
%C A399790 Spanning trees are counted as distinct edge sets; rotations and reflections are not identified. Unlike a knight's tour, a spanning tree may branch.
%C A399790 The one-vertex graph has one spanning tree. The knight graphs for n=2 and n=3 are disconnected.
%C A399790 The initial nonzero values appear in the knight-graph row of Weisstein's Tree Number table.
%H A399790 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A399790/b399790.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..35</a>
%H A399790 D. E. Knuth, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9411240">Leaper graphs</a>, Math. Gazette 78 (1994), 274-297; arXiv:math/9411240 [math.CO] (graph definition and connectivity).
%H A399790 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KnightGraph.html">Knight Graph</a>.
%H A399790 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SpanningTree.html">Spanning Tree</a>.
%H A399790 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TreeNumber.html">Tree Number</a> (initial values in the knight-graph row).
%F A399790 a(1)=1, a(2)=a(3)=0. For n>=4, 0<a(n)^2<=72^(n^2-1), since a row of the reduced Laplacian has squared norm at most 8^2+8.
%e A399790 a(3)=0 because the central square has no legal knight move.
%e A399790 a(4)=144000. The graph has 16 vertices and 24 edges; this is the number of 15-edge subsets that form a connected acyclic graph.
%o A399790 (Python)
%o A399790 from sympy import zeros
%o A399790 def a(n):
%o A399790     moves = [(dx, dy) for dx in (-2, -1, 1, 2)
%o A399790              for dy in (-2, -1, 1, 2) if abs(dx) + abs(dy) == 3]
%o A399790     L = zeros(n*n)
%o A399790     for x in range(n):
%o A399790         for y in range(n):
%o A399790             i = n*x + y
%o A399790             for dx, dy in moves:
%o A399790                 u, v = x + dx, y + dy
%o A399790                 if 0 <= u < n and 0 <= v < n:
%o A399790                     L[i, i] += 1
%o A399790                     L[i, n*u + v] = -1
%o A399790     return L[:-1, :-1].det(method="domain-ge")
%o A399790 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 11)])
%Y A399790 Cf. A033996 (edges), A288951 (queen graphs), A288957 (king graphs).
%K A399790 nonn,new
%O A399790 1,4
